Create Crafts & Additions - modified, unofficial SkyTekx build for Forge 1.20.1
=============================================================================

This is a MODIFIED, UNOFFICIAL version of Create Crafts & Additions. It is not made, supported or
endorsed by MRH0. Please report problems with this build to SkyTekx
(https://github.com/skytekx/skytekx3-1201-server/issues), not to the upstream project.

Original work
-------------
  Create Crafts & Additions by MRH0 and contributors
  Source:   https://github.com/mrh0/createaddition
  Base:     branch 1.20.1 @ 42b6f2d06f0412a7cee787d767449d5b1b3b81b8 (2026-11-02; mod_version 1.3.3
            plus the merged, unreleased upstream changes after the 1.3.3 release; Forge 47)
  Backport: content taken from branch 1.21.1 @ 658a390b8ff4daa17013e9447b29949330c8a42a
            (2026-11-02; mod_version 1.7.3, NeoForge 1.21.1)

Modifications
-------------
  Modified by SkyTekx (Florian Kleber), 2026, for the SkyTekx 3 modpack. The result still runs on
  Minecraft 1.20.1 with Forge 47, keeps the mod id createaddition and is versioned
  1.20.1-1.7.3-skytekx.1.

  Summary of the changes:
  - Build: reproducible jar (no file timestamps, fixed entry order, no build timestamp in the
    manifest); this NOTICE and the upstream LICENSE ship inside the jar; mods.toml marks the build
    as a modified, unofficial one and sends bug reports to SkyTekx.
  - Config: createaddition-common.toml gains the keys of the 1.21.1 CommonConfig at 658a390
    (wires.connector_network_internal_buffer, the sections liquid_blaze_burner and electric_pump,
    and the amulet and capacitor keys in misc). The Liquid Blaze Burner tank default stays
    4000 mB instead of upstream's 1000 mB. Existing values are kept.
  - Network: the channel createaddition:main uses protocol 2, so this build does not connect to
    upstream 1.20.1 builds such as 1.3.3, in either direction. Packet id 2 carries the time
    remaining packet of the goggle timers.
  - Fixes from the 1.21.1 line: the Modular Accumulator capability no longer recurses into a
    StackOverflowError, goggles show the controller's data and schematics keep its size. The
    Liquid Blaze Burner reads its tank and heat capacity from the config, and a switch of fuel
    no longer adds up the burn times. The soundscapes play while Create's ambient sounds are on.
    The death messages of barbed wire and the Tesla Coil are translated in every locale. The
    Electric Motor peripheral rejects NaN and infinite numbers. A mined Electrum Block drops
    itself, needs an iron pickaxe and serves as a beacon base. The girder connector has a valid
    particle texture.
  - Features from the 1.21.1 line: goggle timers for the burn time of the Liquid Blaze Burner
    and the charge time of the Tesla Coil, the stress values of the Electric Motor, Alternator
    and Rolling Mill in the item and goggle tooltips, waterloggable and wrenchable barbed wire,
    paper rolled into straw, the two buckets in forge:buckets, and float results from the
    Digital Adapter peripheral.
  - Balance from the 1.21.1 line: the spool recipe makes 24 spools from iron plates and an iron
    rod.
  - Ignitable fluids from the 1.21.1 line: fluids in the fluid tag forge:ignites (biofuel,
    creosote, crude oil, plant oil, ethanol, gasoline, diesel and biodiesel, where a mod adds them)
    catch fire and burn away, and falling burning fluid spreads the fire while doFireTick is on.
    The mixin config now uses the refmap createaddition.refmap.json.
  - Wires: the energy networks of connectors and redstone relays live in a graph saved per
    dimension (data/createaddition_wires.dat), so energy and relays work across unloaded chunks
    and no wire lookup loads a chunk (upstream 126ed38, 393c51f, 9dd1b46). The graph only trusts
    a saved chunk with the full status and a block entity list (a local change). The operator
    command /cca_wires stats, verify and rebuild (permission level 2) shows, checks and rebuilds
    the graph of a dimension. Wires are culled by the box of all their ends, stay visible while
    their connector is off screen and are drawn to a far end the client has not loaded (126ed38).
    Shears on a connector cut all its wires (3abfa39).
  - Content backported from the 1.21.1 line is listed here as it is added.

  The complete change history is the git history of the ports/createaddition directory of
  https://github.com/skytekx/skytekx3-1201-server
  That directory is the source code of this jar: the exact source of a given jar is that directory
  at the commit that added the jar to local-mods/. ports/createaddition/UPSTREAM.md lists every
  change to the upstream build.

